  "published": "2026-11-15T06:39:46.833Z",
  "releaseNotes": "Kazo OS 3.4.0-preview.1, changes for app developers:\n- The Store offers the newest app version your Kazo OS runs, and a beta OS reads the beta catalog. The Store, kazopkg and the update check no longer offer an app version built for a newer Kazo OS than yours: they pick the newest version that runs here, so an app rebuilt for a newer SDK does not block an older OS. A prerelease of Kazo OS reads the beta channel of the official catalog (catalog-beta.json) and offers the beta versions of the apps; a stable Kazo OS reads catalog.json and never sees them.\n- App repositories call shared workflows and follow new Kazo OS versions by themselves. The kazoos-solution template now generates short workflows that call the reusable workflows of Kazo-ca/Os-AppTemplate (@v1), plus a \"Kazo OS SDK update\" workflow: when Kazo OS releases a version, the app moves to it, runs its CI, and is published (beta branch and beta channel for a pre-release; merged and published for a minor or major release; checked only for a patch). A red CI opens a TODO issue. A beta version (1.2.1-beta.1) goes to the beta channel of the catalog, and .github/scripts/bump-app-version.sh changes the app's version.\n- Kazo OS prereleases are published from the beta branch. Changing the preview number in build/Versions.props on the beta branch publishes a prerelease: Kazo.Os.* packages on nuget.org, a v<version> tag and a GitHub pre-release. main only accepts a stable version and beta only a prerelease version.\nRelease notes: https://github.com/Kazo-ca/Os/releases/tag/v3.4.0-preview.1",
